@article{DiPierro2021PotentialCB, title={Potential Clinical Benefits of Quercetin in the Early Stage of COVID-19: Results of a Second, Pilot, Randomized, Controlled and Open-Label Clinical Trial}, author={Francesco Di Pierro and Somia Iqtadar and Amjad Khan and Sami Ullah Mumtaz and Mohsin Masud Chaudhry and Alexander Bertuccioli and Giuseppe Derosa and Pamela Maffioli and Stefano Togni and Antonella Riva and Pietro Allegrini and Saeed Khan}, journal={International Journal of General Medicine}, year={2021}, volume={14}, pages={2807 - 2816} }
QP statistically shortens the timing of molecular test conversion from positive to negative, reducing at the same time symptoms severity and negative predictors of COVID-19. Background The severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) is the cause of the ongoing global pandemic known as COVID-19.
The role of quercetin and curcumin acting as anti-coronavirus agents is summarized, the lack of clinical trials of their combined use is pointed out, and the use of natural compounds in treating COVID-19 is emphasized.Expand ... Mojtaba Shohan, R. Nashibi, +5 authors A. Khodadadi ... Souparnika H. Manjunath, R. Thimmulappa ... M. Rondanelli, S. Perna, +9 authors A. Riva ... Results are encouraging, but further studies are required to add quercetin as regular prophylaxis, as shown by the value of EXP(B), those who had taken the supplement had a protection factor of 14% more to not contract the COVID-19 infection than that of those whoHad taken a placebo.Expand
